        <mxCell id="PmE4qD0tFPrtIfjssiZb-1" parent="PmE4qD0tFPrtIfjssiZb-12" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=15;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;" value="&lt;b&gt;Business Rationale:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#666&quot;&gt;When oil prices spike (MarketAlertEvent for CL=F, sector &amp;quot;Energy/Commodities&amp;quot;) AND social media buzzes about oil (SocialTrendEvent for &amp;quot;Iran oil strike&amp;quot;, same sector via GlobalKTable metadata), the windowed join detects the correlation. A CorrelatedAlert is more actionable than either signal alone.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="80" width="380" x="550" y="-50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IhFFBlPRyQaCd3sXlYsd-1" parent="PmE4qD0tFPrtIfjssiZb-12" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=10;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=none;glass=0;shadow=0;sketch=1;curveFitting=1;jiggle=2;" value="&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;the correlated alerts must use alerts-with-metadata (the output of the GlobalKTable join), not raw&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; alerts-enriched. The reason is that the KStream-KStream windowed join rekeyes both streams by sector — and the sector field only exists after the metadata enrichment step.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="250" x="660" y="220" as="geometry" />
